# Interviews

Interviews are dialogues that involve asking questions to obtain information about someone’s experience, expertise, beliefs, 
or fitness for a certain position. Interviews can be conducted in person, over the phone, and through the Internet, being either formal or informal. 
They are held for the purposes of obtaining information or giving someone their opinion on a matter.

# Skills 

Skills are abilities which can be acquired through the process of learning and experience that help an individual do things in a proper way. 
Skills can relate to anything that involves methods, knowledge, communication, problem solving, and teamwork.

# Leadership 

Leadership entails having the skills to direct, inspire and help people achieve their common objectives. 
Leadership skills involve giving direction, communication, good judgment and accountability. 
Other elements of effective leadership include listening, establishing trust and enabling others.

# Research 

In its simplest form, research is defined as the methodical study or analysis of information in 
order to find answers to questions, gain deeper insight, or build new knowledge.

# Panels 

A panel can be defined as a group of people who have been brought together for a discussion, 
exchange of views, or to make decisions. In some cases, a panel is a small group of people who 
assess individuals, presentations, or projects.

# Experience 

Experience is what one acquires through being employed and performing their responsibilities 
in the job. This shows the experience that someone has gained in terms of job performance.

# Projects 

A process planned to develop, improve, or maintain a product, system, or service through 
the application of technology requires planning, organizing, employing technical knowledge, 
and evaluation.

# Process 

Progress gives an idea of the amount of work that has been done compared to the total amount 
of work that is supposed to be done.

# President 

Leaders who have been elected or appointed to oversee the activities of the club and represent 
its members. Club presidents help members in achieving their objectives through meetings.


